Name: frameText

Type: property

Syntax: get the frameText of <image>

Summary:
Returns the current <frame> of an <animated GIF> encoded as PNG data.

Associations: image

Introduced: 1.0.0

OS: mac, windows, linux

Platforms: desktop, server

Example:
set the currentFrame of image "myGIF" to tFrame
set the viewerImage of widget "imageViewer" to the frameText of image "myGIF"

Value:
The <frameText> of an <image> is binary data containing the current
frame encoded as a PNG image.
This property is read-only and cannot be set.

Description:
Use the <frameText> <property> to obtain an individual <frame> of an
<animated GIF> as encoded PNG data. The result is suitable for passing
directly to an LCB widget via a binary data property, or for setting on
another image object using "set the text of image".

Set <currentFrame> to the desired frame index before reading this
property.

Use <frameDuration> to obtain the display time for the frame in order to
drive an animation loop:

   on nextFrame
      add 1 to sCurrentFrame
      if sCurrentFrame > the frameCount of image "myGIF" then
         put 1 into sCurrentFrame
      end if
      set the currentFrame of image "myGIF" to sCurrentFrame
      set the viewerImage of widget "imageViewer" to \
         the frameText of image "myGIF"
      send "nextFrame" to me in \
         (the frameDuration of image "myGIF") milliseconds
   end nextFrame

For non-animated images, <frameText> returns the same value as the
<text> property.

References: property (glossary), animated GIF (glossary),
frame (glossary), image (keyword), currentFrame (property),
frameCount (property), frameImageData (property),
frameDuration (property), repeatCount (property)

Tags: multimedia
